{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791286522,"nonce":"iRDaKvqPwp19Z0Cb6gfTJ+sjWd0=","title":"Apply abstract conversions at conditions, nominal targets and map entries","message":"The tiered 845/1094 baseline leaves three concrete gaps in the implicit conversion cluster:\n- Issue9057: a zero-valued abstract with @:to Bool returning true takes the false branch of a switch guard because truth_of never calls the conversion.\n- Issue2661: AChild's @:to ABase is filtered out because ABase is not a primitive target. Native abstract operators also discard their declared operand parameter types, and inlined operators substitute raw operands without retaining a conversion cast.\n- Issue4100: a declared Map\u003cString, ValueAbs\u003e stores raw String and Int literal entries instead of applying ValueAbs's @:from constructors.\n\nAbstractImplicitBoundaries reproduces the condition failure on the baseline and passes the reference Haxe interpreter. It covers if, switch guard, while, do-while, nominal conversions at let/assignment/call boundaries, bodyless and instance operators, and StringMap/IntMap/ObjectMap literal values.\n\nImplementation removes the primitive-only filter from declared @:to rules, runs Bool conversion at condition consumption, preserves formal conversion casts in abstract inlining, and keeps bodyless binary operator signatures while emitting native operations. Map literal lowering applies from/to methods using the expected map entry types. Generic @:from matching and structural constraints remain outside this checkpoint.","files":null}]}